% INVALID certificate (test of the checker), reported by @cruisesong7 in #25: for min x subject to x >= 1/2 with x
% CONTINUOUS, the optimal value is 1/2, but d1 "rounds" x >= 1/2 to x >= 1, which is valid only for an integer
% variable, and so proves the wrong optimal value 1.  A sound checker must reject it.
VER 1.0
VAR 1 x
INT 0
OBJ min 1 0 1
CON 1 0
c1 G 1/2 1 0 1
RTP range 1 1
SOL 1
s1 1 0 1
DER 1
d1 G 1 OBJ { rnd 1 0 1 } -1
